From ef44f34966d20f98b181768f411c613ca395f2cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guodong Xu <guodong.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:18:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: spacemit: k1: Add Zic64b ISA extension

The K1 X60 cores have 64-byte cache blocks, described by their
cbom/cbop/cboz-block-size of 64, so they implement Zic64b.  Declare it in
each core's riscv,isa-extensions and in the deprecated riscv,isa string.

Signed-off-by: Guodong Xu <guodong.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260920-rva23u64-hwprobe-v2-v8-6-5f14bc5c23d3@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Paul Walmsley <pjw@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 1fc72ff0d3fc38759bd050420eefc7aabc18936d)
